# Bitwarden API credentials, for `bw login --apikey`.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: bare KEY=VALUE, no `export`. That keeps this
# usable two ways -- handed to a unit as EnvironmentFile=, and sourced by a
# POSIX shell -- where `export` would have made it shell-only, since systemd
# treats the whole `export BW_CLIENTID` string as a variable name and drops
# the line.
#
# The consequence for shell callers: sourcing this sets the variables in the
# current shell but does NOT put them in the environment of anything it then
# runs. Whoever needs that must export them itself. .github/wsl/oobe.sh already
# does, right after its `. "$BWRC"`.
#
# The quotes stay. systemd strips them, and they keep `.` from word-splitting
# a value that ever contains whitespace.
BW_CLIENTID="{{- (bitwardenFields "item" "vw.regulad.xyz").client_id.value -}}"
BW_CLIENTSECRET="{{- (bitwardenFields "item" "vw.regulad.xyz").client_secret.value -}}"
